  "articleSummary": "The article argues that search is a broad problem space and that semantic/vector search should complement—not replace—exact-match, lexical, and fuzzy search in a hybrid architecture. It explains embeddings, vectors, semantic similarity, and technologies such as pgvector, Qdrant, Weaviate, Pinecone, Milvus, Elasticsearch, and other vector-search systems, comparing their deployment models, capabilities, and workload fit. The intended audience is engineers and technical decision-makers choosing search infrastructure, with an emphasis on understanding when vectors are appropriate rather than blindly embedding everything. Its tone is practical and tutorial-like, framed around making sound technical choices and “winning” search arguments by understanding the full landscape.",
